1. c4 Nf6 2. Nc3 e6 3. e4 d5 4. e5 d4 (4... Ng8 {is also playable.}) 5. exf6
dxc3 6. bxc3 Qxf6 7. d4 c5 8. Nf3 h6 ({This move is unnecessary. Black should
play} 8... cxd4) 9. Bd3 Nc6 10. O-O Be7 11. Qe2 O-O ({Not liking} 11... cxd4
12. cxd4 Nxd4 13. Nxd4 Qxd4 14. Bb2) 12. d5 Na5 13. Ne5 Bd6 14. f4 exd5 15.
cxd5 Re8 {Allowing the queen a useful manoeuvre.} 16. Qe4 g6 17. Qa4 Qd8 18.
Qc2 Bxe5 19. fxe5 c4 {Black probably relied on this since White cannot play
Bxg6 because of ...Qb6+.} 20. e6 Re7 {An alternative was to sacrifice his
bishop for two pawns.} 21. Bxg6 fxg6 22. Qxg6+ Rg7 23. Qf5 {Black is lost. The
rest is easy.} Qb6+ 24. Kh1 Bxe6 25. dxe6 Qc6 26. Rf3 Qe8 27. Bxh6 Qg6 28. Bxg7
Qxf5 29. Rxf5 {Source: "Chess for the Love of It" by A. R. B. Thomas 
(Routledge & Kegan Paul, 1973), p54. Contributed by Ulrich Tamm, 10 January
2023.} 1-0

